    {
      "title": "SecurityFilterChain Configuration",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "SecurityFilterChain Configuration",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Chain Bean",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Declare a ==@Bean SecurityFilterChain== taking `HttpSecurity`",
                "End the method with `http.build()`",
                "{red:WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter} is **removed** in Spring Security 6"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@Bean",
                "SecurityFilterChain filterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {",
                "  http.authorizeHttpRequests(a -> a",
                "    .requestMatchers(\"/public/**\").permitAll()",
                "    .requestMatchers(\"/admin/**\").hasRole(\"ADMIN\")",
                "    .anyRequest().authenticated());",
                "  return http.build();",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "Lambda DSL"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Matching Rules",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Rules match ==top to bottom==, **first match wins**",
                "Put {green:specific} matchers before {orange:broader} ones",
                "Finish with `anyRequest()`"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Checks authority"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`hasRole(\"ADMIN\")`",
                  "`ROLE_ADMIN`"
                ],
                [
                  "`hasAuthority(\"ROLE_ADMIN\")`",
                  "exact string `ROLE_ADMIN`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No prefix in hasRole",
              "text": "`hasRole(\"ROLE_ADMIN\")` is wrong: Spring adds ==ROLE_== itself. Use it only in `hasAuthority`."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Multiple Chains",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`securityMatcher(\"/api/**\")` limits a chain to those paths",
                "Add ==@Order== so the specific chain is checked first",
                "{blue:API chain}: stateless; {green:web chain}: form login"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Password Encoding",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Password Encoding",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Why Hash, and With What",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Never store {red:plain text} or fast hashes (**MD5**, **SHA-1**)",
                "Use an ==adaptive salted hash== via `PasswordEncoder`",
                "Two methods: `encode(raw)` and `matches(raw, stored)`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Encoder",
                "Notes"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`BCryptPasswordEncoder`",
                  "==Standard bean==; strength **10**; salt inside the hash"
                ],
                [
                  "`Argon2PasswordEncoder`",
                  "Memory-hard alternative"
                ],
                [
                  "`SCryptPasswordEncoder`",
                  "Memory-hard alternative"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Delegating Encoder",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`PasswordEncoderFactories.createDelegatingPasswordEncoder()`",
                "Hash is stored as `{bcrypt}$2a$10$...` with an {id} prefix",
                "The prefix picks the algorithm, so ==upgrades keep old hashes working=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@Bean",
                "PasswordEncoder passwordEncoder() {",
                "    return new BCryptPasswordEncoder();",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "or the delegating factory for upgradable hashes"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Checking a Password",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Hashing is ==one-way==: you cannot decode it",
                "Check with `encoder.matches(raw, stored)`",
                "Never `encode(raw).equals(stored)`: each encode uses a **new salt**"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Gotcha",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No PasswordEncoder mapped for the id null",
              "text": "Thrown when there is no `PasswordEncoder` bean, or the stored hash has no `{id}` prefix. Add the bean or prefix the hash, e.g. `{bcrypt}`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "JWT Stateless Authentication",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "JWT Stateless Authentication",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. JWT Anatomy",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==header.payload.signature==, each part **Base64URL**",
                "{red:Signed, not encrypted}: anyone can read the payload",
                "Claims: `sub`, `exp`, `iat`, `roles`",
                "Never put ==secrets== in the payload"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Login and Filter Flow",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Stateless: `STATELESS` session policy, ==CSRF disabled== for token-only APIs",
                "Login calls `AuthenticationManager.authenticate(UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken)`",
                "Returns a signed token with a ==short `exp`=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Login",
                    "sub": "authenticate()",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Signed JWT",
                    "sub": "short exp",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Bearer header",
                    "sub": "every request",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "x",
                    "text": "JWT filter",
                    "sub": "OncePerRequestFilter",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "SecurityContextHolder",
                    "sub": "Authentication set",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "http.csrf(c -> c.disable())",
                "  .sessionManagement(s -> s.sessionCreationPolicy(",
                "      SessionCreationPolicy.STATELESS))",
                "  .addFilterBefore(jwtFilter,",
                "      UsernamePasswordAuthenticationFilter.class);"
              ],
              "note": "filter validates signature and expiry, then builds the Authentication"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Trade-offs",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:No server session}: easy horizontal scaling",
                "{red:No instant revocation} until the token expires",
                "Short-lived access token plus ==refresh token==",
                "Strong signing key, kept in ==config==, not code"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "A JWT is only **signed**. Keep it short-lived and never put ==secrets== inside."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Method Security, CORS and CSRF",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Method Security, CORS and CSRF",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Method Security",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`@EnableMethodSecurity` ==replaces== `@EnableGlobalMethodSecurity`",
                "`@PreAuthorize` checks {green:before} the method; `@PostAuthorize` checks {orange:after} it",
                "SpEL sees arguments and principal: owner-only access",
                "Proxy-based: ==self-invocation is not checked=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole('ADMIN')\")",
                "void purge() { }",
                "@PreAuthorize(\"#id == authentication.principal.id\")",
                "User get(Long id) { }"
              ],
              "note": "second rule: owner-only access"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. CORS vs CSRF",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "CORS",
                "CSRF"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Is",
                  "browser rule, response headers",
                  "token on POST/PUT/DELETE"
                ],
                [
                  "Enable",
                  "`http.cors(withDefaults())` + `CorsConfigurationSource` bean",
                  "**on by default**"
                ],
                [
                  "Off when",
                  "never an auth tool",
                  "only stateless header-token APIs"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Preflight `OPTIONS` must pass ==without credentials==",
                "`allowCredentials(true)` cannot pair with origins `\"*\"`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Gotchas",
              "text": "A CORS error is often a {red:401/403} blocking preflight. CORS is **not** authentication. Disabling CSRF on a session-cookie app is a ==vulnerability==."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**CSRF off when?** Only stateless header-token APIs",
                "**Why is self-invoked @PreAuthorize skipped?** The call bypasses the proxy",
                "**Why does CORS show but the cause is 401?** Security blocks the preflight"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Security Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Security Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Status Codes and Config",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Check",
                "Means"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{red:401}",
                  "not **authenticated**"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:403}",
                  "authenticated but **forbidden**"
                ],
                [
                  "`hasRole('X')`",
                  "authority `ROLE_X`"
                ],
                [
                  "`hasAuthority('X')`",
                  "the ==exact string=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@Bean",
                "SecurityFilterChain filterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {",
                "  http.authorizeHttpRequests(a -> a",
                "    .requestMatchers(\"/admin/**\").hasRole(\"ADMIN\")",
                "    .anyRequest().authenticated());",
                "  return http.build();",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "order rules specific to general"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Passwords and JWT",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`BCryptPasswordEncoder` or `DelegatingPasswordEncoder`",
                "Compare with ==encoder.matches(raw, stored)==, never re-encode",
                "Session policy ==STATELESS==, token in `Authorization: Bearer`",
                "`OncePerRequestFilter` via ==addFilterBefore==",
                "Short expiry plus ==refresh token=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Bearer header",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "JWT filter",
                    "sub": "signature, exp",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "SecurityContextHolder",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Method, CORS, CSRF",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Rules",
              "items": [
                "`@EnableMethodSecurity` + `@PreAuthorize`",
                "CORS via a `CorsConfigurationSource` bean",
                "CSRF off only for ==stateless== header-token APIs"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Common mistake",
              "text": "A CORS error is often a {red:401/403} on the preflight, and disabling CSRF on a cookie app is a hole."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Rules are `/api/**` authenticated, then `/api/public/**` permitAll. An anonymous user calls `/api/public/ping`. Result?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Blocked: login required.",
                "First match wins, so the broad rule catches it.",
                "Put the specific matcher first."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Login always fails. Why? `encoder.encode(raw).equals(stored)`",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Each encode adds a fresh salt, so the strings differ.",
                "Use `encoder.matches(raw, stored)`."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A browser shows a CORS error on POST. The network tab shows the OPTIONS preflight got 401. Fix?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Security rejected the credential-less preflight.",
                "Enable `http.cors(withDefaults())` with a `CorsConfigurationSource` bean."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
